From: nixos-hardware <nixos-hardware@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: machine_restart: try the restart handlers before EFI

On the MT7988 (Banana Pi BPI-R4 Pro) the EFI runtime that U-Boot installs
advertises EFI_RT_SUPPORTED_RESET_SYSTEM, so efi_reboot() is called and the
PSCI restart handler in the restart chain is never reached.  U-Boot's
ResetSystem then fails to reset the SoC, and because do_kernel_restart() sits
behind it the machine prints "Reboot failed -- System halted" and hangs until
the power is cut.

The restart chain is the architecture's own recovery path and should take
precedence over a firmware-provided one; EFI belongs as a fallback for when
nothing else can do it.  Order the two the other way round, so a firmware
ResetSystem that does not work cannot prevent the working handler running.
Capsule-update resets still reach ResetSystem, since the PSCI handler does not
return.

Signed-off-by: nixos-hardware <nixos-hardware@example.invalid>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
index fba7ca1..cb94833 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/process.c
@@ -131,16 +131,18 @@ void machine_restart(char *cmd)
 	local_irq_disable();
 	smp_send_stop();
 
+	/* Now call the architecture specific reboot code. */
+	do_kernel_restart(cmd);
+
 	/*
 	 * UpdateCapsule() depends on the system being reset via
-	 * ResetSystem().
+	 * ResetSystem().  Only fall back to it if the restart handlers above
+	 * declined -- otherwise firmware that implements ResetSystem badly
+	 * prevents the working handler from ever running.
 	 */
 	if (efi_enabled(EFI_RUNTIME_SERVICES))
 		efi_reboot(reboot_mode, NULL);
 
-	/* Now call the architecture specific reboot code. */
-	do_kernel_restart(cmd);
-
 	/*
 	 * Whoops - the architecture was unable to reboot.
 	 */
